{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "command": {
    "translate": {
      "description": "Translate fcitx5-config-vue vue-i18n localization files",
      "template": "Load the translate skill first. The argument is: $ARGUMENTS\n\nIf no argument was provided, print ONLY this usage text and stop:\n\nUsage: /translate <mode>\n  sync     Scan src for new t() strings, add missing keys to src/locales/zh-CN.json, translate them to Simplified Chinese, then propagate the new keys to every other locale file\n  all      Translate all other languages using the English keys + Simplified Chinese as context\n  <lang>   Add a new language or translate an existing one (e.g. ja, ko, de)\n\nThe canonical English strings are the KEYS of each JSON locale file (src/locales/*.json). The English locale itself is auto-generated in src/i18n.ts and has no file. Never change keys when translating — only values.\n\nIf the argument is \"sync\", first collect the current set of message keys from the t() function in the sources:\nnode .opencode/skills/translate/keys.mjs\nFlatten the nested \"language\" object of src/locales/zh-CN.json into dotted keys (e.g. language.Chinese) and compare against the collected keys. Add any new key to src/locales/zh-CN.json as \"English sentence\": \"<Chinese translation>\" (translate it). Then, in every other src/locales/<lang>.json file, add the same new keys with their translated values, and keep the nested language block complete. Report a summary.\n\nIf the argument is \"all\", do NOT run sync. Read src/locales/zh-CN.json (Simplified Chinese) and use the keys as English context, then translate every other locale (ca, da, de, es, fr, he, ja, ka, ko, ru, vi, zh-TW). Only translate values; never change the keys.\\n\\nIf the argument is a language code like ja, ko, de, fr, es, ru, zh-CN, or zh-TW, check whether it is registered in the messages object of src/i18n.ts independently of whether src/locales/<lang>.json exists. If src/locales/<lang>.json exists, do an incremental translation: compare its keys to src/locales/zh-CN.json, translate any missing keys, and fix untranslated values (values still equal to their key). If that existing file is not yet registered in src/i18n.ts (it is still listed as a zhCN fallback), also add \"import <alias> from './locales/<lang>.json'\" where <alias> is an identifier-safe binding of the locale code (e.g. zhTW for zh-TW, removing or camelCasing the hyphen) and point the messages key \"<lang>\" at <alias> (keep the original locale code as the key), removing the previous zhCN fallback line. If the file does not exist, create it by copying src/locales/zh-CN.json, register it in src/i18n.ts (add \"import <alias> from './locales/<lang>.json'\" with an identifier-safe <alias> and point the messages key \"<lang>\" at <alias>, keeping the original locale code as the key, removing the previous zhCN fallback line), then translate the whole file.\n\nAfter translating, validate EVERY locale registered in the messages object of src/i18n.ts except 'en':\nnode .opencode/skills/translate/validate.mjs src/locales/zh-CN.json src/locales/<lang>.json\nDerive the list of locales to validate from the keys of the messages object in src/i18n.ts, excluding only 'en' and the source catalog 'zh-CN' (fall back to the src/locales/*.json files if messages cannot be parsed). Run it for each remaining registered locale, including any newly added ones. Any MISSING/EXTRA key or UNTRANSLATED value must be fixed before finishing."
    }
  }
}
